msgid "{root}\nClassic (recommended): review edits and commands, or trust this folder for quiet local work.\nFlow: edits, moves, deletes and sandboxed shell commands run without questions. Each chat turn is recorded; /undo restores its files while keeping later human changes. Commits of this turn's own files can run quietly.\nSecurity: everything off until you allow it.\nAll modes keep Sentinel, budgets and receipts. Push, secrets, integrations and authority changes still ask or stay off. Flow commands need a verified sandbox; command network stays off."
msgstr "{root}\nClassic (recommended): review edits and commands, or trust this folder for quiet local work.\nFlow: edits, moves, deletes and sandboxed shell commands run without questions. Each chat turn is recorded; /undo restores its files while keeping later human changes. Commits of this turn's own files can run quietly.\nSecurity: everything off until you allow it.\nAll modes keep Sentinel, budgets and receipts. Push, secrets, integrations and authority changes still ask or stay off. Flow commands need a verified sandbox; command network stays off."

# Flow (ADR 0010)
msgid "Flow works on its own: reading, edits, moves, deletes and sandboxed commands run without asking, and a shell is available inside the sandbox. Each turn is recorded so you can undo it with /undo. Push, credentials, provider and authority changes, integrations and network for commands still ask or stay off. Classic is recommended for large work, if you are new to the TUI or want more control; Security is for sensitive files and explicit permissions."
msgstr "Flow works on its own: reading, edits, moves, deletes and sandboxed commands run without asking, and a shell is available inside the sandbox. Each turn is recorded so you can undo it with /undo. Push, credentials, provider and authority changes, integrations and network for commands still ask or stay off. Classic is recommended for large work, if you are new to the TUI or want more control; Security is for sensitive files and explicit permissions."

